{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RCck576s7N8Gi1s4ejzXcA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Crucible Stage 1 â€” Master Plan: Aurora Awareness Revamp\n\n**Plan shape**\n- A 5-wave plan, each wave independently shippable, sequenced by value-per-effort Ã— North-Star urgency: **W1** model surface â†’ **W2** collection fix â†’ **W3** benchmarks â†’ **W4** awareness+value â†’ **W5** minimal adoption. A 6th wave (**W6 Map**) was held IN-but-optional at Stage 0; the Shark Tank recommends deferring it out of this run.\n- Each wave is mapped to the North Star via an inclusion test (NS1â€“NS5). W3 serves NS1/NS2/NS3(fit); W5 serves NS3 and feeds labels toward NS4; W6 scores only \"(weak)\" on NS1.\n\n**Wave 3 â€” Benchmark thin-slice + decision-grade model view (NS2)**\n- Intent: convert the model price-sheet into a decision tool by joining a thin, license-clean benchmark slice, unlocking \"best-for-X\" picks.\n- Sources: ingest OpenRouter `/models` (specs/pricing, **transient-enrich only â€” never redistributed**) plus Epoch AI **CC-BY** benchmarks (GPQA Diamond, SWE-bench Verified, FrontierMath, MATH-L5, AIME).\n- **CC1 no-leak rule is load-bearing:** Epoch CC-BY is redistributable; Artificial-Analysis-derived and OpenRouter-derived data are NOT.\n- Composite is **sparse-aware**: computed only where component coverage exists, with coverage/missing shown explicitly â€” no single black-box index, no false authority over missing cells.\n- Schema blocker (Stage-2 verified): the live `model_benchmarks` table (schema.sql ~291â€“302) had `source_url`/`scored_at`/`observed_at`/`contamination_flag` but **no `source` and no `license` column**, and `benchmark_scraper.py` inserted without them.\n- **Status: GREEN (2026-06-12).** EXECUTE â†’ orchestrator gate â†’ 2 reviewers (E = CC1/CC5 provenance GO; F = ingester/composite/cards NO-GO with 1 BLOCKER + 1 MAJOR and a failing repro) â†’ FIX â†’ re-gate â†’ orchestrator re-verify. Gate moved **1108 â†’ 1120 passed** (+12 additive; 1 pre-existing unrelated `runs` failure left untouched). Migration `0027_benchmark_provenance.sql` adds `source`+`license` (idempotent, schema.sql mirrored); a single insert chokepoint `roles/benchmark_ingest.py::insert_benchmark` enforces CC5. CC1 no-leak verified **both directions through the real publisher**.\n\n**Wave 5 â€” Adoption decision: minimal, honest, label-building (NS3, deliberately small)**\n- Decision content lives in the report: per top candidate, card fields (what-it-is / fit / recommendation+confidence / advantages / risks / provenance / effort) â€” recommendation is a **non-authoritative suggestion, never a consensus verdict**.\n- A `decisions` table records accept/decline/snooze and **doubles as the label source** feeding Wave 2's deferred weight-validation.\n- **No Helping-Hand auto-adoption now** (n=7 forbids automation); accepts get wired into Helping Hand only at **nâ‰¥30**, in a future run.\n- **Status: GREEN (2026-06-12).** EXECUTE â†’ orchestrator gate â†’ 2 reviewers (I = CC1/Â§B-2/anti-test-weakening; J = capture correctness + production-safety; both GO) â†’ 1 bounded hardening FIX â†’ re-gate. Gate moved **1135 â†’ 1152 passed** (+17 additive; same 1 pre-existing unrelated `runs` failure). Delivered migration `0028_decisions.sql` â€” `decisions(id, artifact_id FK, decision_type CHECK IN ('adopt','defer','reject','retire'), reason, explicit_label, explicit_confidence, made_at, made_by_session_id, recorded_at)`.\n\n**Stage 1 approval gate â€” decisions put to John**\n1. Approve the resequenced 5-wave plan (W1â†’W2â†’W3â†’W4â†’W5)? (yes / edit)\n2. W6 Map: Shark Tank recommends **defer**; confirm defer or keep IN as a fenced optional final wave? (defer / keep)\n3. Adoption shrink: OK to skip Helping-Hand auto-adoption now, capture labels + log decisions until nâ‰¥30, then revisit later? (yes / want more now)\n4. Anything to reweight in the wave order?\n\n---\n\nOne flag on grounding: the anchors describe W3 and W5 as already **GREEN/executed (2026-06-12)**, yet present a Stage-1 **approval gate** that is still asking whether to approve the plan. These are internally inconsistent in the source material â€” either the gate text is a retained artifact from before execution, or the GREEN stamps post-date approval. I've reported both verbatim rather than reconciling them; worth confirming which reflects current state."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4260,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9455,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9455},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2f50c46-b6ed-4001-a457-554cc56e1fab","uuid":"68d62079-8e73-4dc8-afba-9e10c12512b1","request_id":"req_011Cc1Hk11Gbjx5HJXC73uJQ"}
